{"doc_id": "wpilib/2026/kinematics/swerve-drive-kinematics", "ord": 0, "library": "wpilib", "version_lo": "2026.2.1", "season": "2026", "channel": "stable", "language": "java", "kind": "prose", "title": "Swerve Drive Kinematics", "heading_path": "Kinematics and Odometry › Swerve Drive Kinematics", "symbol": "edu.wpi.first.math.kinematics.SwerveDriveKinematics", "body": "The SwerveDriveKinematics class converts between a ChassisSpeeds object and several SwerveModuleState objects. Construct it with the locations of each module relative to the robot center as Translation2d objects.\n\n```java\nimport edu.wpi.first.math.kinematics.SwerveDriveKinematics;\nimport edu.wpi.first.math.geometry.Translation2d;\n\nSwerveDriveKinematics kinematics = new SwerveDriveKinematics(\n    new Translation2d(0.381, 0.381), new Translation2d(0.381, -0.381),\n    new Translation2d(-0.381, 0.381), new Translation2d(-0.381, -0.381));\nSwerveModuleState[] states = kinematics.toSwerveModuleStates(speeds);\n```", "source_url": "https://docs.wpilib.org/en/stable/docs/software/kinematics-and-odometry/swerve-drive-kinematics.html", "upstream_rev": "fixture-rev", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T12:00:00Z", "license": "fixture (illustrative, not authoritative)", "trust": "official", "authority": 3}
{"doc_id": "wpilib/2026/kinematics/swerve-drive-kinematics", "ord": 1, "library": "wpilib", "version_lo": "2026.2.1", "season": "2026", "channel": "stable", "language": "java", "kind": "prose", "title": "Swerve Drive Kinematics", "heading_path": "Kinematics and Odometry › Swerve Drive Kinematics › Desaturating wheel speeds", "symbol": "", "body": "After converting ChassisSpeeds to module states, call SwerveDriveKinematics.desaturateWheelSpeeds(states, maxSpeedMetersPerSecond) so that no module is commanded above its physical maximum while preserving the ratio between modules.", "source_url": "https://docs.wpilib.org/en/stable/docs/software/kinematics-and-odometry/swerve-drive-kinematics.html", "upstream_rev": "fixture-rev", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T12:00:00Z", "license": "fixture (illustrative, not authoritative)", "trust": "official", "authority": 3}
{"doc_id": "wpilib/2026/kinematics/swerve-drive-kinematics-cpp", "ord": 0, "library": "wpilib", "version_lo": "2026.2.1", "season": "2026", "channel": "stable", "language": "cpp", "kind": "prose", "title": "Swerve Drive Kinematics (C++)", "heading_path": "Kinematics and Odometry › Swerve Drive Kinematics", "symbol": "frc::SwerveDriveKinematics", "body": "In C++ the class is frc::SwerveDriveKinematics<4>, templated on the number of modules.\n\n```cpp\n#include <frc/kinematics/SwerveDriveKinematics.h>\nfrc::SwerveDriveKinematics<4> kinematics{frontLeft, frontRight, backLeft, backRight};\nauto [fl, fr, bl, br] = kinematics.ToSwerveModuleStates(speeds);\n```", "source_url": "https://docs.wpilib.org/en/stable/docs/software/kinematics-and-odometry/swerve-drive-kinematics.html", "upstream_rev": "fixture-rev", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T12:00:00Z", "license": "fixture (illustrative, not authoritative)", "trust": "official", "authority": 3}
{"doc_id": "wpilib/2027/kinematics/swerve-drive-kinematics", "ord": 0, "library": "wpilib", "version_lo": "2027.0.0-alpha-7", "season": "2027", "channel": "alpha", "language": "java", "kind": "prose", "title": "Swerve Drive Kinematics", "heading_path": "Kinematics and Odometry › Swerve Drive Kinematics", "symbol": "org.wpilib.math.kinematics.SwerveDriveKinematics", "body": "In 2027 the Java packages moved from edu.wpi.first to org.wpilib. SwerveDriveKinematics now lives in org.wpilib.math.kinematics.\n\n```java\nimport org.wpilib.math.kinematics.SwerveDriveKinematics;\n```", "source_url": "https://docs.wpilib.org/en/latest/docs/software/kinematics-and-odometry/swerve-drive-kinematics.html", "upstream_rev": "fixture-rev", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T12:00:00Z", "license": "fixture (illustrative, not authoritative)", "trust": "official", "authority": 3}
{"doc_id": "wpilib/2027/yearly-changelog", "ord": 0, "library": "wpilib", "version_lo": "2027.0.0-alpha-7", "season": "2027", "channel": "alpha", "language": "any", "kind": "release", "title": "New for 2027", "heading_path": "Yearly Overview › New for 2027 › Breaking changes", "symbol": "", "body": "Breaking changes for 2027: Java packages were renamed from edu.wpi.first to org.wpilib and C++ namespaces from frc:: to wpi::. SmartDashboard and SendableChooser are replaced by the Telemetry and Tunables APIs. AprilTag and CameraServer moved to vendordeps. Vendor libraries must be re-imported for 2027 Alpha 7 projects.", "source_url": "https://docs.wpilib.org/en/latest/docs/yearly-overview/yearly-changelog.html", "upstream_rev": "fixture-rev", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T12:00:00Z", "license": "fixture (illustrative, not authoritative)", "trust": "official", "authority": 3}
{"doc_id": "wpilib/2026/command-based/subsystems", "ord": 0, "library": "wpilib", "version_lo": "2026.2.1", "season": "2026", "channel": "stable", "language": "java", "kind": "prose", "title": "Subsystems", "heading_path": "Command-Based Programming › Subsystems", "symbol": "edu.wpi.first.wpilibj2.command.SubsystemBase", "body": "Subsystems are the basic unit of robot organization in the command-based paradigm. Extend SubsystemBase; the CommandScheduler calls periodic() every 20 ms loop.\n\n```java\npublic class Elevator extends SubsystemBase {\n  @Override public void periodic() {}\n}\n```", "source_url": "https://docs.wpilib.org/en/stable/docs/software/commandbased/subsystems.html", "upstream_rev": "fixture-rev", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T12:00:00Z", "license": "fixture (illustrative, not authoritative)", "trust": "official", "authority": 3}
{"doc_id": "wpilib/2026/known-issues", "ord": 0, "library": "wpilib", "version_lo": "2026.2.1", "season": "2026", "channel": "stable", "language": "any", "kind": "release", "title": "Known Issues", "heading_path": "Yearly Overview › Known Issues › Simulation", "symbol": "", "body": "Known issue: the simulation GUI may fail to start on some Linux distributions with Wayland; set the environment variable GDK_BACKEND=x11 as a workaround.", "source_url": "https://docs.wpilib.org/en/stable/docs/yearly-overview/known-issues.html", "upstream_rev": "fixture-rev", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T12:00:00Z", "license": "fixture (illustrative, not authoritative)", "trust": "official", "authority": 3}
{"doc_id": "wpilib/2026/3rd-party-libraries", "ord": 0, "library": "wpilib", "version_lo": "2026.2.1", "season": "2026", "channel": "stable", "language": "any", "kind": "prose", "title": "3rd Party Libraries", "heading_path": "VS Code Overview › 3rd Party Libraries › Installing vendordeps", "symbol": "", "body": "Vendor libraries are installed as vendordep JSON files in the vendordeps/ folder. Use the WPILib VS Code Dependency Manager or run ./gradlew vendordep --url=<jsonUrl>. Each vendordep declares frcYear, which must match the WPILib project year.", "source_url": "https://docs.wpilib.org/en/stable/docs/software/vscode-overview/3rd-party-libraries.html", "upstream_rev": "fixture-rev", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T12:00:00Z", "license": "fixture (illustrative, not authoritative)", "trust": "official", "authority": 3}
{"doc_id": "robotpy/2026/timed-robot", "ord": 0, "library": "wpilib", "version_lo": "2026.2.1", "season": "2026", "channel": "stable", "language": "python", "kind": "code", "title": "TimedRobot (Python)", "heading_path": "RobotPy › Getting Started", "symbol": "wpilib.TimedRobot", "body": "```python\nimport wpilib\n\nclass MyRobot(wpilib.TimedRobot):\n    def robotInit(self):\n        self.timer = wpilib.Timer()\n```", "source_url": "https://robotpy.readthedocs.io/projects/robotpy/en/stable/wpilib/TimedRobot.html", "upstream_rev": "fixture-rev", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T12:00:00Z", "license": "fixture (illustrative, not authoritative)", "trust": "official", "authority": 2}
{"doc_id": "phoenix6/2026/motion-magic", "ord": 0, "library": "phoenix6", "version_lo": "26.1.0", "season": "2026", "channel": "stable", "language": "java", "kind": "prose", "title": "Motion Magic", "heading_path": "Device API › Closed-Loop Control › Motion Magic", "symbol": "com.ctre.phoenix6.configs.TalonFXConfiguration", "body": "Motion Magic is a control mode that generates a trapezoidal or S-curve motion profile on the TalonFX. Configure cruise velocity, acceleration and jerk in TalonFXConfiguration.MotionMagic, then request MotionMagicVoltage.\n\n```java\nvar cfg = new TalonFXConfiguration();\ncfg.Slot0.kP = 60; cfg.Slot0.kV = 0.12;\ncfg.MotionMagic.MotionMagicCruiseVelocity = 80; // rps\ncfg.MotionMagic.MotionMagicAcceleration = 160; // rps/s\ntalon.getConfigurator().apply(cfg);\ntalon.setControl(new MotionMagicVoltage(0).withPosition(10));\n```", "source_url": "https://v6.docs.ctr-electronics.com/en/latest/docs/api-reference/device-specific/talonfx/motion-magic.html", "upstream_rev": "fixture-rev", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T12:00:00Z", "license": "fixture (illustrative, not authoritative)", "trust": "vendor", "authority": 3}
{"doc_id": "phoenix6/2026/canbus", "ord": 0, "library": "phoenix6", "version_lo": "26.1.0", "season": "2026", "channel": "stable", "language": "java", "kind": "release", "title": "New for 2026", "heading_path": "Yearly Changes › New for 2026 › CANBus", "symbol": "", "body": "The <Device>(int id, String canbus) constructors are deprecated in 2026 and will be removed in 2027. Construct a CANBus object and pass it to device constructors instead: new TalonFX(1, new CANBus(\"canivore\")).", "source_url": "https://v6.docs.ctr-electronics.com/en/latest/docs/yearly-changes/yearly-changelog.html", "upstream_rev": "fixture-rev", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T12:00:00Z", "license": "fixture (illustrative, not authoritative)", "trust": "vendor", "authority": 3}
{"doc_id": "phoenix6/releases/26.1.0", "ord": 0, "library": "phoenix6", "version_lo": "26.1.0", "season": "2026", "channel": "stable", "language": "any", "kind": "release", "title": "Phoenix 6 v26.1.0", "heading_path": "Releases › v26.1.0", "symbol": "", "body": "Phoenix 6 v26.1.0: kickoff release for the 2026 season. Requires WPILib 2026.1.1 or newer. Minimum C++ standard is C++20.", "source_url": "https://github.com/CrossTheRoadElec/Phoenix-Releases/releases/tag/v26.1.0", "upstream_rev": "fixture-rev", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T12:00:00Z", "license": "fixture (illustrative, not authoritative)", "trust": "vendor", "authority": 2}
{"doc_id": "revlib/2026/spark-config", "ord": 0, "library": "revlib", "version_lo": "2026.0.0", "season": "2026", "channel": "stable", "language": "java", "kind": "prose", "title": "Configuring a SPARK", "heading_path": "REVLib › SPARK › Configuration", "symbol": "com.revrobotics.spark.SparkMax", "body": "Since REVLib 2025, SPARK motor controllers are configured with configuration objects. Create a SparkMaxConfig, set parameters, then apply it with configure().\n\n```java\nSparkMax max = new SparkMax(3, MotorType.kBrushless);\nSparkMaxConfig config = new SparkMaxConfig();\nconfig.smartCurrentLimit(40).idleMode(IdleMode.kBrake);\nmax.configure(config, ResetMode.kResetSafeParameters, PersistMode.kPersistParameters);\n```", "source_url": "https://docs.revrobotics.com/revlib/configuring-a-spark", "upstream_rev": "fixture-rev", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T12:00:00Z", "license": "fixture (illustrative, not authoritative)", "trust": "vendor", "authority": 3}
{"doc_id": "revlib/2024/cansparkmax", "ord": 0, "library": "revlib", "version_lo": "2024.2.4", "season": "2024", "channel": "stable", "language": "java", "kind": "prose", "title": "CANSparkMax (legacy)", "heading_path": "REVLib 2024 › CANSparkMax", "symbol": "com.revrobotics.CANSparkMax", "body": "In REVLib 2024 the SPARK MAX is controlled with CANSparkMax: new CANSparkMax(3, MotorType.kBrushless); settings are applied with individual setters such as setSmartCurrentLimit(40) and burned with burnFlash().", "source_url": "https://docs.revrobotics.com/revlib/2024/cansparkmax", "upstream_rev": "fixture-rev", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T12:00:00Z", "license": "fixture (illustrative, not authoritative)", "trust": "vendor", "authority": 3}
{"doc_id": "pathplanner/2026/autobuilder", "ord": 0, "library": "pathplannerlib", "version_lo": "2026.1.2", "season": "2026", "channel": "stable", "language": "java", "kind": "prose", "title": "Build an Auto", "heading_path": "PathPlannerLib › Build an Auto › AutoBuilder", "symbol": "com.pathplanner.lib.auto.AutoBuilder", "body": "Configure AutoBuilder once in your drive subsystem constructor with pose supplier, reset pose consumer, robot-relative speeds supplier, a drive output consumer, a PPHolonomicDriveController, the RobotConfig loaded from the GUI settings, and an alliance flip supplier.", "source_url": "https://pathplanner.dev/pplib-build-an-auto.html", "upstream_rev": "fixture-rev", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T12:00:00Z", "license": "fixture (illustrative, not authoritative)", "trust": "vendor", "authority": 3}
{"doc_id": "photonvision/2026/pose-estimation", "ord": 0, "library": "photonvision", "version_lo": "2026.3.4", "season": "2026", "channel": "stable", "language": "java", "kind": "prose", "title": "Using PhotonPoseEstimator", "heading_path": "Programming › PhotonLib › Robot Pose Estimation", "symbol": "org.photonvision.PhotonPoseEstimator", "body": "PhotonPoseEstimator combines AprilTag detections with the field layout to estimate the robot pose. Feed the estimate into SwerveDrivePoseEstimator.addVisionMeasurement with the result timestamp.", "source_url": "https://docs.photonvision.org/en/latest/docs/programming/photonlib/robot-pose-estimator.html", "upstream_rev": "fixture-rev", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-28T12:00:00Z", "license": "fixture (illustrative, not authoritative)", "trust": "vendor", "authority": 3}
